  "delivery": {
    "title": "Delivery and recovery",
    "description": "When a destination accepts a record, that delivery is complete. If it is unreachable, Smeltr retries and pauses input when buffers fill. If it refuses a record, Smeltr follows your chosen action: hold and retry, send it elsewhere for investigation, or count and drop it.",
    "caption": "Choose any normal Smeltr destination to receive refused records for investigation and later replay. Selecting it for this job makes it a dead-letter destination; it is not a separate destination type. Smeltr waits for every selected destination to confirm receipt. If one is unavailable, the input streams sending records to it can still be paused.",
